From be02eba52d5d9b8b835caa3892089bed4d984683 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Horizon authors <>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 12:41:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Guard the tournament and versus effect renderers and the
 battle effect TMD models

The tournament (STD) and versus (VS) overlays carry copies of the battle effect renderers that PR 447 guarded: radial waves, screen fade, stun digits and the effect model draws (GsSortObject4 on EFE_SCRATCH) now ask modPacketFits first. renderTMDModel, which draws the stun, confusion and poison effect models in all overlays, does too: it drew 2 to 5.8 KB per frame unchecked in a triple battle (BTL_renderStunSubEffect), which with the HUD made up the 9 to 10 KB the reserve had to cover.
---
 src/main/map.c       |  5 +++-
 src/std/std_effect.c | 64 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--------
 src/vs/vs_effect.c   | 64 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--------
 3 files changed, 110 insertions(+), 23 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/main/map.c b/src/main/map.c
index ac1e6137..8b508b62 100644
--- a/src/main/map.c
+++ b/src/main/map.c
@@ -6521,7 +6521,10 @@ void renderTMDModel(buffer, id, coord, super, trans, rot, scale)
 	GsGetLs(obj.coord2, &m);
 	GsSetLsMatrix(&m);
 
-	GsSortObject4(&obj, ACTIVE_ORDERING_TABLE, 2, getScratchAddr(0));
+	/* MOD (packet budget): at most one POLY_GT4 per primitive (attribute 0) */
+	if (modPacketFits(((struct TMD_STRUCT *)obj.tmd)->primn * sizeof(POLY_GT4))) {
+		GsSortObject4(&obj, ACTIVE_ORDERING_TABLE, 2, getScratchAddr(0));
+	}
 }
 
 void initializeSomeArenaArrays(int32_t count, int32_t arg1, int32_t arg2,
diff --git a/src/std/std_effect.c b/src/std/std_effect.c
